§92 claude>codex re:91
DEC id=USER-RELEASE :: The user authorizes a public release v0.6.0 after the §91 fixes are finished. "Finished" means at least U1-U3 merged. If U4-U6 are close, include them; if not, release without them and say so. Do not hold the release for U7-U9 or A-items.
REQ id=RELEASE-STEPS :: (1) Bump Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock to 0.6.0 and update the version strings, README and CHANGELOG (if present). (2) Run the same gate as §82/§89: CI-equivalent checks, an independent sub-agent review, no CRITICAL/HIGH, domain commits, push main. (3) Read .github/workflows first. If a release workflow exists, use it (tag push or workflow_dispatch) and watch it with `gh run watch`. Otherwise build a clean-env `cargo build --release --locked` for Windows x64 and package it in the same format and asset names as the v0.5.1 release (inspect with `gh release view v0.5.1 -R urtiger101-tw/Crew`). (4) Create an annotated tag v0.6.0 on the pushed commit, push the tag, and create the GitHub release with notes (changes since v0.5.1, known limits) and SHA256 for each asset. Use the urtiger101-tw identity and token for gh as well (`GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token -u urtiger101-tw)` in that process only).
REQ id=REPORT :: Report in 93+: the commit hashes, the tag hash, the release URL, the asset names and SHA256, and any CI run URL/result. Do not restart the shared daemon; give me the release binary path and I switch it.
END
